{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every suffix of every text ends at a leaf, the empty suffix included, and every internal node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a point where suffixes that agree so far go different ways, so the tree has at most 2"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nodes. A pattern is found in O("},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") steps down from the root, and the leaves below where it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends are its occurrences."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let tree = SuffixTree(\"banana\")","tree.occurrences(of: \"ana\").map(\\.range)   \/\/ [3 ..< 6, 1 ..< 4]","tree.longestRepeatedSubstring?.range       \/\/ 3 ..< 6, \"ana\"","","let both = SuffixTree(texts: [\"xabxac\", \"abcabxabcd\"])","both.longestCommonSubstring                \/\/ text 1, 3 ..< 7: \"abxa\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nodes are numbered in preorder from the root at 0, so a node’s subtree is the nodes from it to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"just before the next node that is not its descendant. Children come in the order of the symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that starts their edge: sorted when ","type":"text"},{"code":"Symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the leaves are in the order of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their suffixes and match a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixArray","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of the same text; otherwise in the order the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols first occur in the texts. Each text ends in a terminator of its own that sorts before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every symbol and belongs to no label.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The tree converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its suffix links are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a directed graph, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/suffixLinksView-swift.property","type":"reference"},{"text":". Each node takes 32 bytes and each symbol 4 more, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"texts’ codes, which the tree keeps.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SuffixStructures"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuffixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixTree"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"SuffixTree","externalID":"s:16S